text:
Most people hack their pumpkins up like some sort of butcher, but Jeanette Paras prefers to paint famous faces on hers.

Paras has been painting celebrities on pumpkins since before Taylor Swift was born (1988, to be exact), and since then, she's turned massive pumpkins into the likes of Miley Cyrus, Prince Harry, Jay Leno and Santa Claus.

[seealso slug="new-york-haunted-buildings"]

This Halloween, Paras painted North Korean leader Kim Jong-un onto a 374-pound pumpkin, which she needed a forklift to help her move it into her workshop.

Here are some photos of Paras' pumpkins from this year and years past.

